# Story: As a truck driver, I want to move my booking to another slot, so that I can keep my container booked when I am running late. Rescheduling moves the booking to the new slot if it has room, frees the place in the old slot, and keeps the same booking reference. Moving to a full slot is refused with SLOT_FULL; moving to the same slot is refused with SAME_SLOT.

@draft
Feature: Rescheduling a Booking

  Scenario Outline: Reschedule to another slot with room
    Given I am a driver
    And I have booked that slot for a valid container
    When I try to move my booking to another slot starting in 30 minutes with room for 1 truck
    Then the change is confirmed and the outcome is "RESCHEDULED"
    And the slot has 1 place left

    Examples:
      | oldSlotTime       | newSlotTime |
      | tomorrow at 09:30 | tomorrow at 10:00 |

  Scenario Outline: Reschedule to a full slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I have booked that slot for a valid container
    When I try to move my booking to another slot starting in 30 minutes with room for 0 truck(s)
    Then the change is refused because "SLOT_FULL"

  Scenario Outline: Reschedule to the same slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I have booked that slot for a valid container
    When I try to move my booking to another slot starting in 30 minutes with room for 1 truck (s)
    Then the change is refused because "SAME_SLOT"

  Scenario Outline: Reschedule to an occupied slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I have booked that slot for a valid container
    When another driver books a different slot for the same container
    And I try to move my booking to their slot
    Then the change is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

  Scenario Outline: Reschedule with invalid input
    Given I am a driver
    And I have booked that slot for a valid container
    When I try to move my booking to another slot starting in -30 minutes (s)
    Then the change is refused because "CHANGE_CUTOFF_PASSED"
